---
description: Enforce i18n usage and prevent hard-coded user-facing strings.
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# i18n and Copy

- Do not hard-code user-facing copy in components or hooks; use `useTranslation()` and keys from `src/locales/en.json` instead.
- When you add a new piece of copy, add a properly namespaced key to `en.json` and use that key in code – do not invent one-off local constants for strings.
- Respect and reuse existing namespaces and key patterns from the events and settings features instead of creating completely new structures.
- Persist language and other user settings through the existing settings APIs and storage helpers, not through ad-hoc localStorage usage.
- If you are touching UI that still has hard-coded text, treat it as an opportunity to migrate that copy into the i18n system rather than adding more hard-coded strings.
